From 67fe9e81f4376eab5fe4ae6eed31775602eb59ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 4 <phase4@openwch.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 06:44:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] RISC-V: test unversioned WCH XW march strings

The WCH 12.2 driver accepts concatenated and underscore bare-XW spellings and preserves the unversioned vendor extension in generated assembly; GAS supplies the xw1p0 object-attribute default. Add regression tests for bare XW and retain explicit XW versions without adding a GCC-side default-version entry.

Behavior specification: tmp/phase4-evidence/s1-official/bare-xw.tsv; tmp/phase4-evidence/s3-round1-xw-accept-final/results.tsv; tmp/phase4-evidence/s3-round1-xw-accept-final/official-rv32imac_xw.s; analysis/toolchain/phase4-diff-inventory.md.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-arch.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-version.c: New test.
---
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-arch.c    | 7 +++++++
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-version.c | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-arch.c
 create mode 100644 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-version.c

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-arch.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-arch.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..431e7fd1e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-arch.c
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+/* { dg-do compile } */
+/* { dg-options "-march=rv32imac_xw -mabi=ilp32 -mriscv-attribute" } */
+
+int foo;
+
+/* GAS supplies the observed xw1p0 default when assembling this attribute.  */
+/* { dg-final { scan-assembler "_xw\"" } } */
diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-version.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-version.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..8a0bf6e0c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/riscv/wch-xw-version.c
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+/* { dg-do compile } */
+/* { dg-options "-march=rv32imacxw9p9 -mabi=ilp32 -mriscv-attribute" } */
+
+int foo;
+
+/* { dg-final { scan-assembler "xw9p9" } } */
